[h2]The whole of VPuppet, free for 100 hours[/h2]
This demo is not a cut-down version. It is the full VPuppet app: live face, body, hand and finger tracking from your webcam, perfect sync, the VPuppet Virtual Camera for Zoom, Meet, Discord and OBS, VMC output, cloth and hair physics, emotes and hotkeys, mic lip sync, 3D environments and the model library. Use it for real streams and calls while you decide.

[h2]How the 100 hours work[/h2]
[list]
[*]The demo counts [b]100 hours of use[/b]. The count is stored with your Steam account, so it is the same on every computer you use.
[*]Nothing is watermarked or limited while the time lasts.
[/list]

[h2]After 100 hours[/h2]
[list]
[*][b]Never mid-stream.[/b] If the hours run out while you're live, that session keeps running. The lock applies the next time VPuppet starts.
[*][b]Tracking output, the virtual camera and VMC output lock.[/b] Your avatar no longer follows you, and other apps stop receiving it.
[*][b]Nothing you made is lost.[/b] The model library still opens, and every model you imported is still there and can be shown in its folder on disk.
[*][b]Buy VPuppet to unlock everything.[/b] The full version uses the same library and settings, so your models, favourites and tuning carry straight over. No re-importing.
[/list]

[h2]Before you start[/h2]
[list]
[*][b]A webcam is required.[/b]
[*][b]Bring your own VRM avatar[/b] (VRM 0.x or 1.0). VPuppet doesn't include one; VRoid Studio makes them for free.
[*]VPuppet's source code is MIT-licensed on GitHub. The Steam version is the signed, ready-to-run build that updates itself through Steam and comes with support.
[/list]
